{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"STORE SCARE — RESOLVED, no blocker. While the 7 parallel gates ran, one gate_status durable read\nreturned verdict 'stale-store' and one MCP show_ticket exceeded 120s, which looked like store\ndivergence. Diagnosis:\n - git shows refs/heads/tickets (cb530119, 2026-08-15) vs origin/tickets (cbb71cf7, 2026-09-02):\n   2492 vs 154520 commits since merge-base 75b82339. The main checkout's tracker worktree\n   .tickets-hotpath-authoritative is pinned at that stale Aug-15 ref.\n - BUT: worktree CLI reads of all 7 tickets return 'unsigned' (healthy), a session-log write\n   round-tripped through the shared store, and a subsequent MCP show_ticket returned the full\n   log with all 4 comments. A later gate_status on the epic also read healthy.\nCONCLUSION: the 'stale-store' was a TRANSIENT reconverge window, not a diverged store; the\nslowness was self-inflicted load (7 concurrent gate LLM runs + my own MCP polling). The stale\nlocal tickets ref is a pre-existing operator condition that rebar does not resolve through.\nACTION: stop polling MCP while gates run; poll with the free local 'review-plan --status' check\ninstead (no LLM, no network). No tracker-maintenance or force needed; nothing bypassed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788313287866358001,"uuid":"01a92dda-b6fd-41ce-ac0d-f58ab917141b"}